        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:38:27Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(release): publish the browser (wasm32) build under /app/ on the Pages site\n\nA `wasm` job in release.yml (ubuntu-24.04, contents: read) builds the\nbrowser shell with web/build-app-wasm.sh --release on the run's tree,\nchecks the page folder and uploads it as the wasm-app artifact. The\n`site` job waits for it with !cancelled() (the publish pattern), places\nthe folder at app/ in the Zola output and re-checks it there before\nupload-pages-artifact. A failed wasm build leaves app/ as the site's own\n\"not part of this copy\" page (site/content/app.md) and a warning naming\nthe missing browser build; docs and release go out anyway.\n\nweb/check-app-page.sh asserts index.html, wasi_shim.js, camcraft-ui.js\nand a real wasm module are present, and refuses root-absolute or\nprotocol-relative URLs and SharedArrayBuffer (Pages has no COOP/COEP).\nThe front page and the guide's first-run page link the app with what\nworks and what does not yet. No new trigger.\n\nFixes #1103\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
