      "message": "fix(release): the front page claims the browser build only when it was deployed\n\nReview of 612a5d89. The site job appends `app = true|false` to the\ngitignored site/version.toml before zola build: true only when the wasm\njob succeeded, its artifact downloaded (now continue-on-error) and\nweb/check-app-page.sh passes on it. The front page shows \"Open CamCraft X\nin your browser\" only then, \"The browser version of CamCraft X is not\navailable\" otherwise, and the local-preview line without the file.\n\nThe check on the copy at public/app/ is no longer fatal for the docs: a\nfailure drops the copy, flips the flag and rebuilds the site with the\nsame warning annotation. Front-page and first-run wording in plain\nEnglish; the first-run page (Markdown, cannot read the flag) points at\nthe front page instead of claiming the build.\n\nRefs #1103\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
